💼 Software Developer Salary Prediction (Stack Overflow 2020)
This Streamlit web application predicts software developer salaries based on inputs like country, education level, and years of professional experience. It also provides data visualizations from the 2020 Stack Overflow Developer Survey to help users explore salary trends globally.

📊 Dataset
Source: Stack Overflow Developer Survey 2020

Files Used:

survey_results_public.csv: Cleaned survey responses (main dataset)

survey_results_schema.csv: Schema for the survey questions

so_survey_2020.pdf: Official survey questionnaire

The dataset includes responses from developers worldwide, gathered between Feb 5 – Feb 28, 2020.

🚀 Features
🔍 Explore Page
Pie chart of responses by country

Bar chart of mean salary by country

Line chart of mean salary by experience (in years)

🤖 Predict Page
Input: Country, Education Level, Years of Experience

Output: Estimated annual salary in USD

🛠 Tech Stack
Frontend: Streamlit

Backend: Scikit-learn model (RandomForestRegressor)

Language: Python

Libraries: pandas, numpy, matplotlib, pickle, scikit-learn

📁 Project Structure
bash
Copy
Edit
├── app.py                     # Streamlit app entry point
├── predict_page.py           # Prediction page logic
├── explore_page.py           # Data visualization logic
├── saved_steps.pkl           # Pickled model & label encoders
├── survey_results_public.csv # Main dataset
├── survey_results_schema.csv # Dataset schema
├── so_survey_2020.pdf        # Survey questions PDF
└── SalaryPrediction.ipynb    # Jupyter Notebook for training
🧠 Model Training Overview
The model is trained on:

Country

Education Level

Years of Professional Coding Experience

Preprocessing:
Removed nulls and outliers (Salary < 10,000 or > 250,000)

Mapped low-frequency countries to "Other"

Simplified education levels

Converted experience values (e.g., "Less than 1 year" → 0.5)

Model:
Algorithm: RandomForestRegressor

Serialized with: pickle (stored in saved_steps.pkl)

